# QBIT NOVA C

**Creator:** Universal Dragon Aslam  
**Project:** QBIT NOVA C  
**Purpose:** A small C-based quantum-style language, bytecode VM, state-vector simulator, and virtual QMSG/QCPU layer.

QBIT NOVA C does **not** claim that a normal phone or Raspberry Pi becomes a physical quantum computer.

Instead, it builds a **software virtual quantum processor layer** on top of classical hardware.

## Current Capabilities

- `.qn` language syntax
- Lexer, parser, AST, compiler
- Bytecode VM
- Safe action adapter contract
- Qbit simulation
- Hadamard gate
- CNOT simulation
- Entangle simulation
- Repeat blocks
- 2-qbit state-vector core
- Unified `qnova` runner
- QMSG virtual packet layer
- QMSG virtual qbit register view

## Version Timeline

| Version | Feature |
|---|---|
| v1.0 | 2-qbit state-vector core |
| v1.1 | `.qn` to state-vector pipeline |
| v1.2 | Unified `qnova` runner |
| v1.3 | QMSG virtual packet layer |
| v1.4 | QMSG virtual qbit register view |

## Example: Bell State

```qbit
@nova.v1
@qbit.enabled
@quantum.state2

qbit q = |0>
qbit p = |0>

hadamard q
cnot q p

measure q
say q
say p
